WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.520 --> 00:00:03.860
Hello.

2
00:00:03.880 --> 00:00:10.300
I'm a professor of psychiatry at Seoul
National University Bundang Hospital.

3
00:00:10.520 --> 00:00:17.200
Today I'll show you how to fill in the
mood journal, item by item, with examples.

4
00:00:18.670 --> 00:00:21.350
Our mood is a lot like the weather.

5
00:00:21.370 --> 00:00:26.390
There are sunny days, cloudy days, and stormy days.

6
00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:32.510
The mood journal is a small tool for
recording this weather of the mind, every day.

7
00:00:32.730 --> 00:00:40.610
As records build up, you can see your condition
objectively, and notice early signs of relapse.

8
00:00:41.880 --> 00:00:46.040
Fill it in in the evening, as the day winds down.

9
00:00:46.260 --> 00:00:51.240
Keep the journal next to your medication,
and write right after you take it,

10
00:00:51.260 --> 00:00:52.910
so you don't forget.

11
00:00:53.130 --> 00:00:56.950
If a score is hard to pick, compare with yesterday.

12
00:00:56.970 --> 00:01:00.770
If you missed a day, fill it in as soon as you can.

13
00:01:00.990 --> 00:01:04.770
Once you're used to it, 30 seconds a day is enough.

14
00:01:06.240 --> 00:01:11.080
One sheet holds a whole month, and
each day fills one vertical column.

15
00:01:11.800 --> 00:01:17.570
From the top: mood, then emotional
reactivity, motivation, and thinking,

16
00:01:17.590 --> 00:01:24.660
then daily records such as sleep and alcohol,
and finally life events and your lifestyle score.

17
00:01:26.030 --> 00:01:28.370
This is the most important part.

18
00:01:28.390 --> 00:01:32.950
Mood is scored from -4 to +4, in nine steps.

19
00:01:33.870 --> 00:01:40.110
In the evening, look back on your day, pick
the one box that best represents today,

20
00:01:40.130 --> 00:01:41.290
and check it.

21
00:01:41.510 --> 00:01:44.790
Each box has a short description beside it.

22
00:01:44.810 --> 00:01:47.050
Use it as a guide.

23
00:01:47.270 --> 00:01:52.830
Zero means you feel at ease, and you got
through what you needed to do as usual.

24
00:01:53.050 --> 00:01:59.130
Two things guide your choice of score: how
much your daily functioning has changed,

25
00:01:59.150 --> 00:02:02.290
and whether people around you would notice.

26
00:02:03.760 --> 00:02:09.700
-1: You feel indifferent and a little low in
motivation, but you still get things done.

27
00:02:09.720 --> 00:02:14.110
You feel it, but people around you barely notice.

28
00:02:14.330 --> 00:02:20.370
For example, a day when you did your work
as usual, but somehow nothing was fun.

29
00:02:20.890 --> 00:02:25.710
-2: People around you can see that you look depressed.

30
00:02:25.730 --> 00:02:31.150
Daily life is slightly disrupted,
but with effort you can keep going.

31
00:02:31.370 --> 00:02:38.460
A day when you barely dragged yourself to work,
and a coworker asked if something was wrong.

32
00:02:38.980 --> 00:02:43.940
-3: You can't go to school or work, or do housework.

33
00:02:43.960 --> 00:02:47.730
Even with effort, your functioning clearly drops.

34
00:02:47.950 --> 00:02:53.590
For example, you end up missing work
and spend most of the day lying down.

35
00:02:54.110 --> 00:02:58.990
-4: You can't even look after
yourself, like washing or eating.

36
00:02:59.010 --> 00:03:05.180
Severe anxiety, restlessness, or thoughts
of suicide mean you need care from others.

37
00:03:05.400 --> 00:03:11.261
At this point, before filling in the journal,
ask for help right away: your doctor,

38
00:03:11.281 --> 00:03:17.750
an emergency room, or the
suicide prevention hotline, 109.

39
00:03:19.320 --> 00:03:22.600
A rising mood doesn't show up only as joy.

40
00:03:22.620 --> 00:03:29.300
It can also appear as overflowing
energy, touchiness, and irritability.

41
00:03:29.520 --> 00:03:35.640
So the question isn't whether you felt good,
but how different you are compared with usual.

42
00:03:36.260 --> 00:03:41.880
+1: You feel better than usual, with
more motivation, or sometimes irritable,

43
00:03:41.900 --> 00:03:43.740
but people around you don't know.

44
00:03:43.760 --> 00:03:48.490
If you concentrate, you do what
you need to without mistakes.

45
00:03:48.710 --> 00:03:55.110
For example, a day when you were full of
energy and got through a backlog of tasks.

46
00:03:55.630 --> 00:04:00.990
+2: You talk more, feel full of
confidence, or get more irritable,

47
00:04:01.010 --> 00:04:03.890
and people around you say you seem different.

48
00:04:03.910 --> 00:04:08.510
Daily life is slightly disrupted,
but with effort you can keep going.

49
00:04:08.730 --> 00:04:13.930
A day when a family member asked,
why are you talking so much lately?

50
00:04:14.450 --> 00:04:20.650
+3: You take on more than you can handle,
and end up with arguments, legal trouble,

51
00:04:20.670 --> 00:04:23.910
overspending, or impulsive trips.

52
00:04:24.130 --> 00:04:28.590
For example, you bought several
expensive things you hadn't planned,

53
00:04:28.610 --> 00:04:32.810
and had a big fight with the
family who tried to stop you.

54
00:04:33.330 --> 00:04:39.790
+4: You may act violently, or
have hallucinations or delusions.

55
00:04:39.810 --> 00:04:43.610
Hospitalization is needed, so
get medical help right away.

56
00:04:44.580 --> 00:04:48.760
Some days your mood swings so much
that one score can't describe it.

57
00:04:48.980 --> 00:04:51.640
On those days, check Mixed state,

58
00:04:51.660 --> 00:04:56.130
and also check both the highest
and the lowest score of the day.

59
00:04:56.650 --> 00:05:03.090
For example, if you felt up in the morning
at +1, and down in the afternoon at -2,

60
00:05:03.110 --> 00:05:06.130
check both boxes and Mixed state.

61
00:05:07.700 --> 00:05:14.060
From the next rows on, you write a
number from -4 to +4 instead of a check.

62
00:05:14.080 --> 00:05:18.680
The reference point is you when you feel at ease: zero.

63
00:05:19.300 --> 00:05:26.990
Emotional reactivity covers fear, timidity,
worry, and anxiety, and irritability and anger.

64
00:05:27.210 --> 00:05:32.740
If you feel anxious about things you'd
normally let pass, that's the plus side.

65
00:05:32.960 --> 00:05:39.000
+1 if you only felt it inside; +2 if
it showed in your words or actions;

66
00:05:39.020 --> 00:05:45.690
+3 if others could easily tell; +4
if you were completely overwhelmed.

67
00:05:46.310 --> 00:05:50.310
Conversely, if you can't feel the worry you should, say,

68
00:05:50.330 --> 00:05:56.030
you're not worried at all with a deadline
around the corner, that's the minus side.

69
00:05:56.250 --> 00:06:02.210
Having no worries may sound good, but too
much of it can lead to impulsive behavior,

70
00:06:02.230 --> 00:06:03.970
so be careful.

71
00:06:04.490 --> 00:06:07.510
Irritability and anger work the same way.

72
00:06:07.530 --> 00:06:12.490
+1 if you were bothered but held
back; +2 if you expressed it; +3

73
00:06:12.510 --> 00:06:17.540
if it caused conflict; +4 if it
led to abusive words or violence.

74
00:06:18.160 --> 00:06:25.290
If nothing bothered you in a situation where
anyone would get angry, that's the minus side.

75
00:06:25.510 --> 00:06:31.970
On days when nothing like that happened,
think about how you would have felt if it had,

76
00:06:31.990 --> 00:06:34.250
and write that down.

77
00:06:35.620 --> 00:06:42.870
Motivation covers interest, enjoyment,
spending and plans, and your activity level.

78
00:06:43.090 --> 00:06:48.630
If interest, enjoyment, spending,
and appointments have increased,

79
00:06:48.650 --> 00:06:53.210
that's plus; if they have decreased, minus.

80
00:06:53.430 --> 00:07:00.510
If you're spending so much time, energy,
and money that it's a burden, that's +3.

81
00:07:00.930 --> 00:07:04.971
If you don't even want to watch your favorite
show and canceled every appointment,

82
00:07:04.991 --> 00:07:07.863
that's about -2 or -3.

83
00:07:07.883 --> 00:07:11.370
If you did nothing, feeling empty, it's -4.

84
00:07:11.590 --> 00:07:14.810
Activity level is how much you moved your body.

85
00:07:14.830 --> 00:07:20.830
Lying down all day is -4; moving
until you're exhausted is +4.

86
00:07:22.200 --> 00:07:26.390
For thinking, look at speed, amount, and content.

87
00:07:26.610 --> 00:07:32.730
If your thoughts race on and on, with many
ideas and a lot of talking, that's plus.

88
00:07:32.750 --> 00:07:36.700
If they slow down and won't come, that's minus.

89
00:07:36.920 --> 00:07:41.200
If others would have trouble following you, +3.

90
00:07:41.220 --> 00:07:46.140
If even you can't keep up and feel confused, +4.

91
00:07:46.660 --> 00:07:51.900
As for content, if everything seems like it
will go well and you're full of confidence,

92
00:07:51.920 --> 00:07:52.780
that's plus.

93
00:07:52.800 --> 00:07:56.460
In severe cases, you may even feel you're special.

94
00:07:56.680 --> 00:08:02.640
Conversely, if nothing seems like it will
work and your confidence drops, that's minus.

95
00:08:02.660 --> 00:08:07.230
In severe cases, you may feel guilty or want to die.

96
00:08:08.600 --> 00:08:13.254
For hours of sleep, write the hours you slept.

97
00:08:13.274 --> 00:08:17.950
If you fell asleep at midnight
and woke at 7 a.m., write 7.

98
00:08:18.570 --> 00:08:22.630
Sleeping less or more is an
important sign of a mood change.

99
00:08:22.650 --> 00:08:28.830
In particular, if you sleep little but
don't feel tired, your mood may be rising.

100
00:08:29.050 --> 00:08:31.910
Record your weight in kilograms every Sunday.

101
00:08:31.930 --> 00:08:38.070
For menstruation, check every day from
the first day of your period to the last.

102
00:08:39.440 --> 00:08:42.960
For alcohol, write how many drinks you had.

103
00:08:42.980 --> 00:08:46.510
If you had three glasses of soju, write 3.

104
00:08:46.730 --> 00:08:53.550
Binge eating, pain and physical symptoms,
crying, hyperventilation and panic attacks,

105
00:08:53.570 --> 00:08:57.330
and exercise: just check the days they apply.

106
00:08:57.550 --> 00:09:00.950
For example, check Pain on a day with a bad headache,

107
00:09:00.970 --> 00:09:06.690
and Panic attack on a day when you suddenly
felt short of breath and your heart pounded.

108
00:09:08.060 --> 00:09:12.680
For life events, check the days something
happened that could affect your mood,

109
00:09:12.700 --> 00:09:16.500
and briefly write the date and what happened below.

110
00:09:16.720 --> 00:09:22.480
For example, if you argued with a
coworker on the 7th, check the 7th box,

111
00:09:22.500 --> 00:09:27.870
write 7 in the parentheses below,
and write "Argued with a coworker."

112
00:09:28.590 --> 00:09:34.770
Hard things like moving or a breakup, and
good things like a vacation or a promotion,

113
00:09:34.790 --> 00:09:38.180
can all shake your mood, so write both.

114
00:09:39.550 --> 00:09:44.970
At the end of the month, look back on the
month with the Healthy Lifestyle Checklist,

115
00:09:44.990 --> 00:09:47.830
and write down the total score.

116
00:09:48.050 --> 00:09:55.730
Taking medication consistently is 40 points,
regular sleep is 20, and regular exercise is 10.

117
00:09:55.950 --> 00:10:02.750
Getting sunlight, avoiding alcohol, managing
relationships, avoiding excessive activity,

118
00:10:02.770 --> 00:10:09.110
monitoring your mood, and being kind to
yourself are 5 points each, for 100 in all.

119
00:10:09.830 --> 00:10:11.650
Aim for 80 or more.

120
00:10:11.670 --> 00:10:16.089
You can also score it easily with
the QR code on the checklist.

121
00:10:17.559 --> 00:10:19.379
Here is a month filled in.

122
00:10:19.399 --> 00:10:24.479
Connect the checks, and you can see
the flow of your mood at a glance.

123
00:10:26.099 --> 00:10:31.899
In this example, mood rose at the start of
the month, when sleep dropped to 4 to 5 hours,

124
00:10:31.919 --> 00:10:36.739
and around the 19th, when a
vacation cut sleep to 3 hours.

125
00:10:37.759 --> 00:10:41.379
Knowing your own warning signs
helps you head off a relapse.

126
00:10:41.399 --> 00:10:44.539
Please bring your journal to your appointments.

127
00:10:45.909 --> 00:10:51.229
If a paper journal is hard for you,
you can use the web mood journal.

128
00:10:51.249 --> 00:10:54.349
The items are the same as on paper.

129
00:10:54.569 --> 00:10:59.779
Tap a box to choose your mood, and pick
scores and hours of sleep from a list.

130
00:10:59.999 --> 00:11:06.439
Choose one plus box and one minus box,
and Mixed state is checked automatically.

131
00:11:06.459 --> 00:11:10.279
For life events, tap the box and write.

132
00:11:10.899 --> 00:11:14.279
Sign up with the number on the business card I gave you,

133
00:11:14.299 --> 00:11:17.919
and your care team can view it with you.

134
00:11:17.939 --> 00:11:22.919
Don't enter personal information,
and back up your records regularly.

135
00:11:24.389 --> 00:11:27.149
The mood journal is not a test.

136
00:11:27.169 --> 00:11:32.269
There's no right answer; just
honestly pick the closest score.

137
00:11:32.889 --> 00:11:34.949
Missing a day is fine.

138
00:11:34.969 --> 00:11:37.279
Just pick it up again.

139
00:11:37.799 --> 00:11:42.159
Small daily records add up to a healthier tomorrow.

140
00:11:42.979 --> 00:11:46.959
The Department of Psychiatry
at Seoul National University

141
00:11:46.979 --> 00:11:51.159
Bundang Hospital sincerely wishes you a good recovery.

142
00:11:51.179 --> 00:11:52.409
Thank you.
